From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: fail boot on an invalid uc_region, lock the instance scan

Two fixes from one series, carried as one:

1. iris_vpu_boot_firmware() polls CTRL_STATUS while the firmware boots.
   On an invalid uc_region report the poll loop broke out early with the
   count below max_tries, so the timeout check was false and the function
   returned 0. The caller then enabled host interrupts and used firmware
   that never came up. The uc_region error path now returns an error.
2. iris_check_session_supported() walked core->instances without
   core->lock. A concurrent iris_close() takes the lock, unlinks an
   instance and frees it, so the lockless walk could follow a freed
   pointer (a use-after-free at STREAMON). The walk now holds core->lock,
   as iris_check_core_mbpf() does, and drops it before calling that.

Fixes: abf5bac63f68 ("media: iris: implement the boot sequence of the firmware")
Fixes: bdbe1cac0c10 ("media: iris: add check whether the video session is supported or not")
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: Bryan O'Donoghue <bod@kernel.org>

Applied by Bryan O'Donoghue as f301102c17f2 and 428e6f95e685, bodies
identical; taken from the Steam Frame kernel's sm8650-7.2 branch
(e286f5725, 60415b4a4), which cherry-picked them.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c        | 6 +++++-
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c
index 3719f4152..48d34ccbd 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c
@@ -56,10 +56,14 @@ static int iris_check_session_supported(struct iris_inst *inst)
 	bool found = false;
 	int ret;
 
+	mutex_lock(&core->lock);
 	list_for_each_entry(instance, &core->instances, list) {
-		if (instance == inst)
+		if (instance == inst) {
 			found = true;
+			break;
+		}
 	}
+	mutex_unlock(&core->lock);
 
 	if (!found) {
 		ret = -EINVAL;
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
index 3c6ec276f..853425ccc 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vpu_common.c
@@ -84,7 +84,7 @@ int iris_vpu_boot_firmware(struct iris_core *core)
 		ctrl_status = readl(core->reg_base + CTRL_STATUS);
 		if ((ctrl_status & CTRL_ERROR_STATUS__M) == 0x4) {
 			dev_err(core->dev, "invalid setting for uc_region\n");
-			break;
+			return -EINVAL;
 		}
 
 		usleep_range(50, 100);
